 and fields  so many that it's not really clear what  the thing is doing anymore and this  happens sometimes if you have something  like a utilities class  rather than thinking oh this method that  i want to create  what object does this go with best like  i've certainly made the mistake of like  oh let's just put this in the utilities  class and this and this and then at one  point this is like this  this very very big blob of functionality  where some parts might actually rather  live  in a different class where they belong  better  the opposite of a large class is a lazy  class  so you can also have a class that's just  a little bit of data maybe  one or two functions that also didn't  really  doesn't really help readability because  then of course your code base gets  divided also over different  files because classes often live in the  wrong files so if you have  a little bit of functionality in a class  that's also a sign  that maybe something could be  restructured a bit  other smells that are commonly occurring  in code are  the duplicated code smell this is also  called  code cloning where you have  slightly different versions of the same  code or  sometimes it can also be exactly the  same code in different  places in the code base and this is an  issue because if you want to make a  change to one of the clones  then maybe you also want to make the  same change to other clones and you  might forget like where the  cool clone code is located so lots of  duplication  in a code base is also a sign that  something might be off  the final code smell i want to talk  about today in this video  is message chaining a message chaining  is a  code smell in which one function calls  another function and that function  then calls another  function and that calls another function  and very often it isn't just calling  functions  but it's also passing a blob of data so  i'm calling a function with a parameter  and then the next function is also  taking in this parameter 